"The patient, a 68-year-old male with a PSA of 11.7 and a clinical T1c stage, was assessed using the Cox model for recurrence risk. The model predicts a time to recurrence of 52.0 months, with no observed event during the follow-up period. This prediction reflects the current clinical staging and biomarker status, though long-term recurrence risk remains subject to individual biological variability and follow-up limitations."